    cover_note='Welcome back. In Session 9 we saw how AI goes wrong: it invents, misses the right source, repeats bias, obeys hidden instructions and drifts, and we built a routine to check it. Until now a person always stood between the AI’s answer and the world. Today that changes, because an agent can act: send the email, pay the supplier, adjust the machine. Our question is the one every leader must answer before switching one on: what may an AI agent do on its own, and who approves? We start with an energy company, build the idea one picture at a time, tour six industries, watch two recorded runs, and then set a level of freedom for each entry in your portfolio.',
