        dict(kind='practice', section='Hands-on', title='Give each portfolio entry a level of freedom, and fill a Tool Boundary Sheet for one', minutes=25, label='Hands-on: your portfolio',
             task='Decide how much each of your AI uses may do on its own.',
             steps=['Give every entry a level from 0 to 4.', 'Pick one that would act, and list its keys.', 'Mark what a person approves and what it must never do.', 'Name the owner, the log and the off switch.'],
             output='A level for each entry and one Tool Boundary Sheet.',
             example=dict(kind='l10_portfolio'),
             notes='For twenty-five minutes you work on your own organisation, and I walk round. Open your AI Opportunity Portfolio. Today’s column is the level of freedom. For every entry so far, write a level from zero to four: answers, suggests, drafts, acts then reports, or acts alone. Most should sit at one or two. Then pick one entry that would act, and fill a Tool Boundary Sheet for it from the Templates folder: for read, write, send and spend, what it may do, what a person approves and what it must never do. Finish with the owner, the log and the off switch. The example on the right is for Nile Valley Foods, our fictional distributor: reminders for overdue invoices, at level two.'),
        dict(kind='decision', section='Decision', title='How much freedom would you give your first agent?',
             question='For the entry you just bounded, which level would you allow first?',
             options=[dict(head='Level 1', text='It suggests; your people act. For advice and planning.', icon='speech'),
                      dict(head='Level 2', text='It drafts; a person approves each act. For emails and orders.', icon='check'),
                      dict(head='Level 3', text='It acts, then reports. Only for steps that can be undone.', icon='notebook'),
                      dict(head='Not yet', text='No owner, no off switch or no written keys. Wait.', icon='shield')],
             record='Write the entry, the level, the keys it needs, and the one key you will never give.',
             notes='With your entries marked, one decision. For the entry you just bounded, which level would you allow first? Level one, where it suggests and your people act, suits advice and planning. Level two suits emails, reminders and orders: it drafts and a person approves each act. Level three suits only steps that can be undone and are read in a log, like the cement kiln. And if there is no owner, no off switch or no written keys, the answer is not yet. That is a sound answer, because Robodebt shows what happens when a system acts alone and nobody checks. Say your entry and your level aloud, then write the keys it needs and the one key you will never give.'),
